 &lt;h4 class="mb-1"&gt;Hire Me as an Intern&lt;/h4&gt;
 &lt;p&gt;At the end of high school, I created a website to express my desire to find a summer internship abroad. The website gained massive attention, becoming the #1 post on Y Combinator's Hacker News and attracting over 30,000 visitors in a single day. It also brought me more than 150 emails from around the world and significant media coverage.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Education &amp; Awards</title><link>https://www.marekdlugos.com/education-awards/</link><pubDate>Mon, 13 Apr 2020 18:05:30 +0200</pubDate><guid>https://www.marekdlugos.com/education-awards/</guid><description>&lt;section&gt;
 &lt;h2&gt;Education&lt;/h2&gt;
 &lt;div class="row"&gt;
 &lt;div class="col-md-3"&gt;
 &lt;h3&gt;The Story&lt;/h3&gt;
 &lt;/div&gt;
 &lt;div class="col-md-9"&gt;
 &lt;p&gt;High-quality technical education abroad has been my aim for a long time, which is why I left my home country after
 graduating from the best tech high school in Slovakia (according to the INEKO ranking).&lt;/p&gt;
 
 &lt;p&gt;Followed by applying for the Ivy League universities. The University of Cambridge, according to rankings, the 4th best
 university in the world, invited me for interviews where I exceeded their expectations in Computer Science but didn't
 persuade them with my math skills.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title/><link>https://www.marekdlugos.com/podcast/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.marekdlugos.com/podcast/</guid><description>&lt;!doctype html&gt;
